ation and in vitro cloning of procyclic culture forms of <italic>Trypanosoma brucei</italic> in a semi-defined medium.</article-title><source>Acta Trop</source><volume>36</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>292</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">43092</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000455-Hesse1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hesse</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Selzer</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Muehlstadt</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Duszenko</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>A novel cultivation technique for long-term maintenance of bloodstream form trypanosomes in vitro.</article-title><source>Mol Biochem Parasitol</source><volume>70</volume><fpage>157</fpage><lpage>166</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7637696</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000455-Cross1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cross</surname><given-names>GAM</given-names></name><name><surname>Manning</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><year>1973</year><article-title>Cultivation of <italic>Trypanosoma brucei</italic> sspp. in semi-defined media.</article-title><source>Parasitology</source><volume>67</volume><fpage>315</fpage><lpage>331</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4761771</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000455-Cross2"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cross</surname><given-names>GAM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1975</year><article-title>Identification, purification and properties of clone-specific antigens constituting the surface coat of <italic>Trypanosoma brucei</italic>.</article-title><source>Parasitology</source><volume>71</volume><fpage>393</fpage><lpage>417</lpage><p